# --- [port] build artifacts: .NET / MSBuild (build outputs for this Playbook) ---
# Write both upper and lower case. **The migration target Linux is case-sensitive**,
# so "bin/" alone would miss "Bin/" (whereas Windows/macOS treat them as the same, hiding the gap).
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/

# Publish artifacts
publish/
[Pp]ublish[Oo]utput/
*.publishsettings

# User / IDE specific
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
.vs/
.vscode/
*.DotSettings.user

# Test / coverage
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
*.coverage
*.trx

# IaC (CDK etc.)
cdk.out/
.cdk.staging/
cdk.context.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ⚠️ Do NOT ignore these (if lost during migration, the loss goes unnoticed)
#   - Migrations/          … EF Core Migrations are source code. Ignoring them loses the
#                            schema-change history and removes them from the expected-list check
#   - appsettings*.json    … Configuration is not a build artifact. **Do not put secrets in it**
#   - runtimes/            … Bundled native-dependency binaries. Normally under bin/ and therefore
#                            ignored, but the expected list (build gate) verifies their presence
#                            (→ verify-snippets.md §2)
